# Soma's search, pulled down from home (105+). Bugs from the 135 check on Boss's phone: "dicsord" (two letters
# swapped) didn't find Discord; recent searches never showed when nothing was opened; name searches brought rows of
# unrelated photos. The emulator has no Discord: Chrome and Settings stand in.
# Each pull is checked by the app's own log line (139: a terminal tile that still held the focus made every pull
# open nothing, the Mac Pro's 138 walks). Typing on home is no way in: it searches the app list, not this.
# A clean start: no shade or dialog left by an earlier walk.
shell cmd statusbar collapse
# The Soma keyboard, as on Boss's phone: Gboard autocorrects "chorme" before search sees it (reinstalls reset the IME).
ime dev.omalauncher.boss/dev.omalauncher.keyboard.OmaKeyboardService
key BACK
key HOME
wait 1500
# Home pressed on home opens the app list with its search field and keyboard (as the gesture bar's swipe up does, on
# purpose): one Back puts the keyboard away, a second the list; else the first pull only closed the list (the Mac Pro,
# 139/140). On home already, a Back does nothing.
key BACK
wait 600
key BACK
# Home settled first.
wait 2000
clearlog
# Pull search down from the middle of home.
swipe 0.5 0.35 0.5 0.75 400
wait 1500
log home pull search
type chorme
wait 1500
expect Chrome
shot typo-finds-chrome
key BACK
key BACK
wait 800
# Put away without opening anything: still a recent search.
clearlog
swipe 0.5 0.35 0.5 0.75 400
wait 1500
log home pull search
expect Recent searches
expect chorme
shot recent-searches-shown
key BACK
key BACK
wait 800
clearlog
swipe 0.5 0.35 0.5 0.75 400
wait 1500
log home pull search
type setitngs
wait 2500
expect Settings
# Look: no row of unrelated photos under Settings.
shot typo-finds-settings-no-photo-noise
key BACK
key BACK
wait 800
# Quick, Files, Photos (Boss, 2026-10-24: "Apple Store" brought a flood of files and photos). A new search opens on
# Quick: apps, people, the calculator and the web, no files and no photos.
clearlog
swipe 0.5 0.35 0.5 0.75 400
wait 1500
log home pull search
expect Quick mode, selected
type apple store
wait 2500
absent Photos & videos
absent On the Mac Pro
absent In files
absent Looking through
shot quick-apple-store-no-files-or-photos
# Files, asked for: the words stay; it looks through files (here and on the Mac Pro) and nothing else.
tap Files mode
wait 2500
expect Files mode, selected
expect apple store
absent Photos & videos
shot files-mode-keeps-the-words
# Photos, asked for: the words stay; photos and videos only.
tap Photos mode
wait 3000
expect Photos mode, selected
expect apple store
absent On the Mac Pro
absent In files
shot photos-mode-keeps-the-words
key BACK
key BACK
wait 800
# Put away on Photos and opened again: Quick again, nothing typed.
clearlog
swipe 0.5 0.35 0.5 0.75 400
wait 1500
log home pull search
expect Quick mode, selected
absent Photos mode, selected
# (The words put away unopened are a recent search now, by design: the row shows them, the field is empty.)
shot reopened-on-quick
key BACK
key BACK
# Soma Notes in search (2026-10-24): needs Soma Notes on the emulator with the walk's notes (notes.walk leaves
# "Sideways book" in its folder). In Notes, every word of a note's title or text; in Quick, titles only.
clearlog
swipe 0.5 0.35 0.5 0.75 400
wait 1500
log home pull search
tap Notes mode
type lighthouse
wait 2500
expect Sideways book
expect Soma Notes · Walk
shot notes-mode-finds-text
tap Sideways book
wait 2500
# Opened in Soma Notes, on that note.
expect Sideways book
shot notes-opened-from-search
key HOME
wait 1000
key BACK
key BACK
[phone] Tap the terminal tile on home, leave it (Back), then pull search down from the middle of home: it opens with the keyboard, and stays (it did nothing before 139).
[phone] Search "dicsord": Discord comes first, and no row of unrelated photos.
[phone] Search "andrew" (a contact): the contact with Call/Text, and no row of unrelated photos.
[phone] Search "beach", then tap Photos: his beach and marina photos show. On Quick (where every search opens) no photos show.
[phone] Search "Apple Store": Quick shows the app and the web, no files or photos; Files lists matching files (names first, then the Mac Pro's, then what is in them); the words stay when switching; a new search opens on Quick.
[phone] Type a search, put search away without opening anything, pull it down again: the search is under Recent searches.
